[size=4][b]Slow Sailing Bagpipes[/b][/size]

Bring bagpipe music aboard your next voyage! Music starts when your boat rows slowly forward or backward, with smooth fades and support for your own MP3, OGG and WAV tracks.

[size=4][b]Now multiplayer compatible[/b][/size]

Helmsmen and passengers, including players standing on deck, hear bagpipes while their own boat rows at an eligible speed. Players ashore or on other boats keep their normal music behavior. Leaving the boat stops playback immediately.

[b]This mod is client-side. Every player who wants to hear the bagpipes needs the mod and audio tracks installed on their own computer.[/b] Players without the mod can join normally and hear vanilla music. Installing it only on the host or dedicated server does not send custom audio to other players. The server does not need the mod.

Each player's track selection and playback are independent; music is not synchronized between clients.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Music starts after about 0.1 seconds of slow forward or backward rowing.
[*]Includes the helmsman and standing or seated passengers.
[*]1.5-second fade-in and 0.5-second fade-out when rowing stops.
[*]Resume rowing on the same boat within 10 seconds to continue the paused track.
[*]Custom MP3, OGG and WAV tracks, with random selection and looping.
[*]Follows the in-game Master and Music sliders, plus the mod's volume setting.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Install BepInEx 5.4.2350 or later, then extract the archive's BepInEx folder into your Valheim installation. Keep SailingBagpipes.dll and the BagPipesTracks folder together under BepInEx/plugins. Repeat on every client that wants to hear the music.

Add non-empty MP3, OGG or WAV files to BagPipesTracks and restart the game after changing the track library. Volume and the track directory can be configured in BepInEx/config/eh.mataeo.valheim.slowsailingbagpipes.cfg.

